claim(0x173b30,'Takes RCX=context, RDX=two float4 endpoints, R8=output float4, R9=output polygon WORD, and stack argument5=category. If context BYTE+229 is zero, transforms both input float4s by matrix+164; then constructs local origin and end-minus-start, forcing both stored W values to1. It collects candidates and tests triangle/quad polygons. Successful primitive points compete by strict XYZ squared distance below initial float32(1e14); equal distances keep the first. It always writes polygon FFFF on no selection and leaves caller point unchanged. On selection, optional matrix+100 transforms the chosen float4 and it returns AL=1. No t value is exported.','Only retained, readable tables and finite, coherent affine inverse/forward matrices justify treating the output as a world-segment point, subject to float32 rounding. There is no local inverse-pair or finite validation. Query success alone establishes neither actor clearance nor safe placement. Body was already captured in the earlier actor-query study; this is a fresh byte-identical capture with stronger whole-chain models.',(0x18b4d0,0x1a8f20,0x13f900,0x1741c0))
claim(0x18b4d0,'Uses XYZ dot products: dn=dot(normal,direction); ordered dn>=0 rejects. It computes t=(dot(normal,vertex0)-dot(normal,origin))/dn and rejects ordered t>1 or t<0. Otherwise it writes float32(origin+t*direction), forces output.W=1, then tests polygon edges. Endpoints0/1 are inclusive. Edge rejection returns false after writing that output. COMISS unordered behavior lets a NaN denominator/t pass these gates under masked exceptions.','This primitive output is a temporary inside173B30. A NaN primitive result is not selected by the enclosing strict distance test. No normalized normal, finite validation or exception-mask guarantee is claimed. Reconfirmed earlier body; decompiler comparison spelling alone is insufficient for unordered behavior.',(0x140200,0x13fcc0,0x13fce0,0x18b760))
